    "question": "Mabel has 5 daisies in her garden, and each daisy has 8 petals.  If she gives 2 daisies to her teacher, how many petals does she have on the remaining daisies in her garden?",
    "gold": "24",
    "answer": "The total number of petals Mabel has in her garden is 5 x 8 = <<5*8=40>>40 petals.\nThe total number of petals that Mabel gives to her teacher is 2 x 8 = <<2*8=16>>16 petals.\nThe total number of petals remaining in her garden is 40 - 16 = <<40-16=24>>24 petals.\n#### 24"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many petals Mabel has on the remaining daisies in her garden, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of petals on all 5 daisies.\n2. Determine the number of daisies Mabel has after giving 2 daisies to her teacher.\n3. Calculate the total number of petals on the remaining daisies.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total number of petals on all 5 daisies.\nEach daisy has 8 petals, so the total number of petals on 5 daisies is:\n\\[ 5 \\times 8 = 40 \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine the number of daisies Mabel has after giving 2 daisies to her teacher.\nMabel originally has 5 daisies and gives 2 to her teacher, so she has:\n\\[ 5 - 2 = 3 \\]\ndaisies left.\n\nStep 3: Calculate the total number of petals on the remaining daisies.\nEach of the remaining 3 daisies has 8 petals, so the total number of petals on the remaining daisies is:\n\\[ 3 \\times 8 = 24 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of petals on the remaining daisies in Mabel's garden is \\(\\boxed{24}\\).",
